# Canonical source for /etc/tbound/net-sink.nft (root:root 0644), the guest side of the net-sink/v1
# command-cell delta (design B2). Loaded by `tbound trial reset` (root) before every trial, through
# `nft -f -` as one atomic transaction, and read back before the service is told so
# (PROVISIONING-SIGNING.md, R5-5).
#
# net-sink/v1 runs the P command cell in the guest ROOT network namespace (Podman --network=host,
# rootless). Two independent layers then confine what the cell can reach:
#   1. inside the cell, Landlock allows TCP connect to port 8080 only and denies bind and every other
#      connect (cmd/tbound-cell-entrypoint);
#   2. this rule, outside the cell: every packet created by a socket in the net-sink cgroup is dropped
#      unless it is TCP to 127.0.33.1:8080, for every protocol and both address families.
#
# The match is by cgroup, not by uid: the cell runs as the service uid (tbound-pi), the same uid whose
# service process makes the provider HTTPS calls, and those sockets must stay untouched. The service puts
# every net-sink command cell under one fixed, persistent parent cgroup,
#   /sys/fs/cgroup/system.slice/tbound-pi.service/cells/net-sink
# (D09NetSinkCgroupName under the cells cgroup of the signed template). nft resolves the path to a cgroup
# id when the rule is LOADED: the directory must exist before `nft -f`, and a recreated directory (or a
# reboot) has another id, so the rule would then match nothing. `tbound trial reset` therefore creates
# the directory if it is absent, reloads this file every time, and attests the load (boot id, parent
# inode, this file's digest) in /run/tbound/net-sink.attest. The service only opens the directory (it
# never creates or removes it) and refuses net-sink when it is absent or the attestation does not match.
#
# The file is idempotent: the first `table` line creates the table when it is absent, so the following
# `delete table` cannot fail, and the third statement recreates it. The whole file is one transaction,
# so a reload replaces the table without a window in which the cgroup is unconfined.
#
# Level and path: the path is relative to the cgroup2 mount (no leading slash, no /sys/fs/cgroup). The
# level is the depth of that cgroup below the cgroup2 root, which is the number of path components:
# system.slice / tbound-pi.service / cells / net-sink = 4. Every descendant (the command scope, the
# libpod scope of the container) matches through this ancestor. A different cells path in the signed
# template needs a different line here: piruntime.D09NetSinkNftMatch derives both values from the
# template, and a unit test holds this file to it.
table inet tbound_net_sink
delete table inet tbound_net_sink
table inet tbound_net_sink {
	chain output {
		type filter hook output priority filter; policy accept;
		socket cgroupv2 level 4 "system.slice/tbound-pi.service/cells/net-sink" ip daddr 127.0.33.1 tcp dport 8080 accept
		socket cgroupv2 level 4 "system.slice/tbound-pi.service/cells/net-sink" counter drop
	}
}
